# rtw88 on the RTOS line, the AP role (A1-A3): the RTL8821CU becomes a 2.4 GHz
# AP (SSID rtos-8821-ap, ch5/2432, HT20, open), the Pi's MT7921AU joins it, and
# the data plane is proven both ways.
#
# The AP MLME is the imported NXP hostapd (CONFIG_HOSTAP_AP); mac80211 keeps the
# AP state machine in the stack and rtw88 pushes the beacon to the firmware
# through its reserved-page path (rtw_fw_download_rsvd_page +
# rtw_send_rsvd_page_h2c, on BSS_CHANGED_BEACON).  The station's own C5/C6
# ladder is not this image: the card is beaconing a BSS, not joining one.
#
# What this profile is not: the phase table (a throughput verdict needs its own
# pre-registration), WPA2, 5 GHz, monitor, and the station role.
#
# The driver + stack are a GPL-2.0 link product; the imported hostapd is
# BSD-3-Clause and the rtw8821c firmware is redistributed with the image
# (docs/LICENSES.md).

CONFIG_BACKEND_FREERTOS=y
CONFIG_OPT_O2=y
CONFIG_PROFILE_BASE=y
CONFIG_CASES="tick rtw88_ap"
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211=y
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_PCI=n
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_SDIO=n
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_USB=y
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_CFG80211=y
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_MAC80211=y
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_RTW88=y
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_NET_LWIP=y
CONFIG_HOSTAP_AP=y
CONFIG_FREERTOS_HEAP_SIZE=16777216
CONFIG_LKPI_USB_CHERRYUSB_STAGE_SIZE=32768
CONFIG_LKPI_USB_CHERRYUSB_STAGE_SLOTS=16
CONFIG_RUNNER_STACK_KB=32
CONFIG_RTW88_USB_BUS=1
